{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d32fd3251dbb5a91", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "These pre-tax contributions and their investment earnings will not be taxed until you withdraw the money, typically after you retire.", "question": null, "answer": "403(b) and 457(b) plans are employer-provided, tax-deferred retirement savings programs. They let participants contribute pre-tax money from their paychecks to invest in certain products. The contributions and investment earnings generally are not taxed until the money is withdrawn, often after retirement.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1134, "output_tokens": 172}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d32fd3251dbb5a91", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "These pre-tax contributions and their investment earnings will not be taxed until you withdraw the money, typically after you retire.", "question": "When are contributions and investment earnings in 403(b) and 457(b) plans generally taxed?", "answer": "They are generally taxed when you withdraw the money, rather than when you make the pre-tax contributions or while the earnings remain in the account.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1134, "output_tokens": 166}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d32fd3251dbb5a91", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Some employers offer both 403(b) and 457(b) plans and allow you to contribute to both plans.", "question": "Misconception: If your employer offers both a 403(b) and a 457(b), you must choose only one plan.", "answer": "Correction: Some employers offer both plans and allow employees to contribute to both. Check with your employer to find out whether both are available.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1134, "output_tokens": 174}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:6e18e63b74ca4992", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "403(b) vs. 457(b) Employer Eligibility", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Employers such as public educational institutions (public schools, colleges, and universities), certain non-profits, and churches or church-related organizations may offer 403(b) plans.  Employers such as state and local government agencies and certain non-profit organizations may offer 457(b) plans.", "question": null, "answer": "Employer eligibility differs between these plans. Public educational institutions, certain nonprofits, and churches or church-related organizations may offer 403(b) plans. State and local government agencies and certain nonprofits may offer 457(b) plans. Because some employers offer both, check with your employer to learn which plans are available to you.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1136, "output_tokens": 217}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:6e18e63b74ca4992", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "403(b) vs. 457(b) Employer Eligibility", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Employers such as public educational institutions (public schools, colleges, and universities), certain non-profits, and churches or church-related organizations may offer 403(b) plans. Employers such as state and local government agencies and certain non-profit organizations may offer 457(b) plans.", "question": "What types of employers may offer 403(b) plans, and what types may offer 457(b) plans?", "answer": "Public educational institutions, certain nonprofits, and churches or church-related organizations may offer 403(b) plans. State and local government agencies and certain nonprofits may offer 457(b) plans. Some employers offer both, so check with your employer to learn which plans are available.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1136, "output_tokens": 296}}
{"id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:6e18e63b74ca4992", "source_id": "aa5c193dcbe9e385", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-accounts/tax-advantaged-accounts/retirement-savings/403b-and-457b-plans", "topic": "403(b) and 457(b) Plans", "subtopic": "403(b) vs. 457(b) Employer Eligibility", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Some employers offer both 403(b) and 457(b) plans and allow you to contribute to both plans.", "question": "Misconception: Any employer that offers a 403(b) plan must also offer a 457(b) plan.", "answer": "Not necessarily. Some employers offer both plans, but the source does not say that every employer offering one must offer the other. Check with your employer to find out which plans are available.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1136, "output_tokens": 249}}
